{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00203",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.52,
      "end_seconds": 5.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Oh, good afternoon, doctor, the receptionist said you'd see me now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.37,
      "end_seconds": 11.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.0,
      "end_seconds": 16.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.31,
      "end_seconds": 31.62,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "Hmm, honestly, it's trouble hearing in my left ear, and my family pushed me to come. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.01,
      "end_seconds": 35.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.82,
      "end_seconds": 41.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "For two years, I'd say. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.31,
      "end_seconds": 45.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.46,
      "end_seconds": 47.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.16,
      "end_seconds": 48.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.42,
      "end_seconds": 81.01,
      "duration_seconds": 30.59,
      "text": "Uh, uh, as for feeling of fullness in the ear, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Right, I've had difficulty following conversation in crowds too, for about a month. Hmm, as for difficulty following conversation in crowds, I'd say moderate. I've been turning the TV up too, for four weeks. So, with turning the TV up, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.34,
      "end_seconds": 84.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.68,
      "end_seconds": 87.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "So, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.91,
      "end_seconds": 91.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Any dizziness or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.65,
      "end_seconds": 97.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "No. None of those, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.44,
      "end_seconds": 104.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any discharge or facial weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.44,
      "end_seconds": 108.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.11,
      "end_seconds": 112.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.75,
      "end_seconds": 115.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.18,
      "end_seconds": 118.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.86,
      "end_seconds": 124.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Well, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.46,
      "end_seconds": 129.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.94,
      "end_seconds": 132.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Okay, so my sister has thyroid problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.23,
      "end_seconds": 141.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.44,
      "end_seconds": 160.38,
      "duration_seconds": 17.94,
      "text": "Losartan. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day. Glycomet. I take it 500 milligrams, twice a day. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I take furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 161.58,
      "end_seconds": 168.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the furosemide was 80 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.95,
      "end_seconds": 172.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Alright. Did you bring the up-to-date prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.88,
      "end_seconds": 179.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.65,
      "end_seconds": 186.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.63,
      "end_seconds": 201.25,
      "duration_seconds": 13.62,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for about a year now. Sorry, uh, I know I'm rambling a bit. I've had diabetes, yes. Yes, heart failure. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.67,
      "end_seconds": 208.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "I see. So, yes, I can see the diabetes in your file as well. Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.0,
      "end_seconds": 211.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.35,
      "end_seconds": 213.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Alright, any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.81,
      "end_seconds": 217.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.94,
      "end_seconds": 220.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.9,
      "end_seconds": 228.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.13,
      "end_seconds": 248.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Okay: temperature 36.6, pressure 123 over 71, pulse 86."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.56,
      "end_seconds": 250.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.62,
      "end_seconds": 254.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.19,
      "end_seconds": 259.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.65,
      "end_seconds": 260.35,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.0,
      "end_seconds": 264.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.37,
      "end_seconds": 286.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "There's a lot of wax in the left ear canal, I can't see the drum."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.39,
      "end_seconds": 288.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.71,
      "end_seconds": 291.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.95,
      "end_seconds": 311.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "The right ear canal and drum are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.38,
      "end_seconds": 313.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.59,
      "end_seconds": 343.48,
      "duration_seconds": 26.89,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Putting it all together, it fits best with hearing loss from wax. I'd also keep an inner ear problem in mind. We should do a hearing test for hearing loss. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.22,
      "end_seconds": 376.96,
      "duration_seconds": 29.74,
      "text": "I'd like you to take ear drops, three times a day, for five days. It's for wax softening. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Please don't use cotton buds or ear candles, they push the wax in further. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.3,
      "end_seconds": 385.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.88,
      "end_seconds": 387.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.79,
      "end_seconds": 393.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.96,
      "end_seconds": 395.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.78,
      "end_seconds": 402.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.31,
      "end_seconds": 406.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}